1. [MAJOR] tests/doc_blocks_test.rs:260 — run_block spawns rb with Command::output() and no timeout, kill, or stdout/stderr cap, so a doc block that loops, sleeps, or prints forever hangs CI or OOMs the harness — add a timeout with child.kill() and a byte cap.
2. [MAJOR] tests/doc_blocks_test.rs:517 — the FRAGMENT arm is an empty block that never executes anything, so a working or broken program misfiled as excerpt/network stays green forever — execute fragments and assert they do not exit 0, or validate the reason prefix.
3. [MAJOR] tests/doc_blocks_test.rs:508 — the RUNS oracle asserts only outcome.exit_ok and ignores stdout, so a doc example that exits 0 while printing the wrong value still passes — snapshot stdout per RUNS entry.
4. [MAJOR] tests/doc_blocks_test.rs:272 — Outcome keeps only the first stderr line starting with Error and check_known_fail compares only that line, so wording, span, or second-line regressions go undetected — record and compare full normalized stderr.
5. [MAJOR] tests/doc_blocks_test.rs:66 — MINIMUM_BLOCKS is 97 while the checked-in buckets total 101, and the floor check is measured >= 97, so deleting up to 4 blocks plus their rows stays green — bump the floor to 101 and assert exact equality.
